    "raw": "Heat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n298.15-2000 K: $Cp^{0} = 7.541 + 3.210 \\times 10^{-3} T - 0.290 \\times 10^{5} T^{-2}$ \n$H^{\\circ}-H_{298}^{\\circ}=7.541\\times10^{-3}T+1.605\\times10^{-6}T^{2}+0.290\\times10^{2}T^{-1}-2.488$ \nReaction equations (kcal/mol): \n298.15-2000 K: $\\Delta \\mathrm{Hr}^{\\circ} = -19.494 - 3.086 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} + 1.026 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 11.350 \\mathrm{T}^{-1}$ \n$\\Delta Gr^{\\circ} = -19.494 + 3.086 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T} \\ln \\mathrm{T} - 1.026 \\times 10^{-6} \\mathrm{T}^{2} + 5.675 \\mathrm{T}^{-1} - 10.687 \\times 10^{-3} \\mathrm{T}$ \nSources: Enthalpy of formation at 298 K from Wagman (126). Other data from Chase (17). ",
